  "verbalization": "Nifurpirinol appears to interact with C8166 through multiple distinct biological pathways, each involving a different target enzyme or protein. The drug is shown to target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10 and 2B15, which are enzymes involved in the metabolism of various compounds, including Sennoside D and Aeruginosin DA722, both of which are known to interact with C8166. This suggests that Nifurpirinol may modulate the metabolic clearance of these compounds, potentially influencing their biological activity or toxicity. Additionally, Nifurpirinol is implicated in targeting the G(I)/G(S)/G(O) subunit gamma-2, a component of G-protein coupled receptors, which is targeted by Isocurcumenol, another compound that acts on C8166. These findings collectively indicate that Nifurpirinol may exert its effects on C8166 through diverse mechanisms, possibly by modulating enzyme activity or receptor function. The consistent presence of C8166 as a target across multiple pathways underscores the potential for Nifurpirinol to influence cellular processes related to drug metabolism and receptor signaling, though further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct relationship.",
